    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Chota Nagpur Plateau is frequently referred to as the 'Ruhr of India' owing to its rich mineral deposits.",
        "Digboi in Assam holds historical significance as the oldest operating oil field and refinery in India.",
        "Jharia (Jharkhand) and Raniganj (West Bengal) are critical exam topics as primary producers of coking coal.",
        "Bauxite is the primary aluminum ore, with Odisha holding the largest reserves in India."
      ],
